IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-part12-retrenchment`

-- Employment Act 1968, s 96A and its enforcement (ss 101(3), 102(5), 126A(aa),
-- 126B(1)(aa), 126C(6), 126D) -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the
-- law. No Gazette notification under s 96A and no regulations were retrieved;
-- where a case needs one, its effect is a supplied fact, and any amount used is
-- illustrative only.

GIVEN `in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `covers` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `workforce` IS A NUMBER, `retrenched` IS A NUMBER, `met` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A RetrenchmentFacts
DECIDE `an exercise` `in force` `applies` `covers` `workforce` `retrenched` `met` IS
    RetrenchmentFacts WITH
        `a notification under section 96A(1) is in force` IS `in force`
        `the notification applies to the employer or to a class the employer is in` IS `applies`
        `the notification requires information on this retrenchment` IS `covers`
        `number of employees the employer has` IS `workforce`
        `number of employees retrenched` IS `retrenched`
        `number of retrenched employees for whom every requirement was met` IS `met`

§ `REQ-0289 (Haziq scenario, event h065)`

-- 40 employees, 12 retrenched in one exercise. Must it notify? Under the Act,
-- only if a Commissioner's Gazette notification applies to it and covers this
-- retrenchment. With none, the Act alone imposes no duty.
#ASSERT NOT `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` (`an exercise` FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 12 0)
-- A notification in force that does not reach this employer, or this retrenchment: still no duty.
#ASSERT NOT `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` (`an exercise` TRUE FALSE TRUE 40 12 0)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE FALSE 40 12 0)
-- One that applies and covers it: the duty is owed (s 96A(2)).
#ASSERT `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 0)
-- Within what time, and with what particulars? The Act does not say: both are
-- whatever the notification specifies. So is the "5 or more" threshold.
#ASSERT `where the answer is fixed` `the time for reporting` EQUALS `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
#ASSERT `where the answer is fixed` `the particulars to be given` EQUALS `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
#ASSERT `where the answer is fixed` `which retrenchments must be reported` EQUALS `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
#ASSERT NOT (`where the answer is fixed` `the time for reporting` EQUALS `the Act itself`)

§ `96A(1) -- the rest of what is delegated`

#ASSERT `where the answer is fixed` `which employers must report` EQUALS `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
#ASSERT `where the answer is fixed` `the form of the report` EQUALS `a Gazette notification by the Commissioner under section 96A(1)`
#ASSERT `where the answer is fixed` `the amount of an administrative penalty` EQUALS `the amount prescribed under section 126B(1)`
#ASSERT `where the answer is fixed` `the maximum fine for disobeying a direction` EQUALS `the Act itself`

§ `96A(2) -- the Act draws no line on size`

-- A 4-person firm retrenching 1, under a notification that covers it, owes the
-- same duty as the 40-person firm: any line is the notification's, not the Act's.
#ASSERT `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 1 0)
-- Nobody retrenched, nothing to report.
#ASSERT NOT `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 0 0)

§ `96A(2) -- compliance, counted employee by employee`

-- All 12 reported in time, in form, with every particular: complied.
#ASSERT `the employer has complied with section 96A(2)` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 12)
#ASSERT `the retrenched employees for whom a requirement was not met` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 12) EQUALS 0
-- 9 of 12: three failures (12 - 9 = 3).
#ASSERT NOT `the employer has complied with section 96A(2)` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 9)
#ASSERT `the retrenched employees for whom a requirement was not met` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 9) EQUALS 3
-- No notification: nothing reported, still complied, because there was no duty.
#ASSERT `the employer has complied with section 96A(2)` (`an exercise` FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 12 0)

§ `126A(aa), 126B(1)(aa) -- civil contravention and penalty occasions`

#ASSERT `there is a civil contravention under section 126A(aa)` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 9)
#ASSERT NOT `there is a civil contravention under section 126A(aa)` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 12)
#ASSERT NOT `there is a civil contravention under section 126A(aa)` (`an exercise` FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 12 0)
-- One occasion per employee: none of 12 reported gives 12 occasions; 9 of 12 gives 3.
#ASSERT `the occasions a contravention notice may cover under section 126B(1)(aa)` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 0) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the occasions a contravention notice may cover under section 126B(1)(aa)` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 9) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the occasions a contravention notice may cover under section 126B(1)(aa)` (`an exercise` FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 12 0) EQUALS 0
-- With an ILLUSTRATIVE prescribed amount of 1,000 (not the real figure, which
-- was not retrieved): 12 x 1,000 = 12,000; 3 x 1,000 = 3,000.
#ASSERT `the most the administrative penalties could total` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 0) 1000 EQUALS 12000
#ASSERT `the most the administrative penalties could total` (`an exercise` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 12 9) 1000 EQUALS 3000

§ `101(3), 102(5) -- outside the returns offence and the secrecy rule`

#ASSERT NOT `section 101(1) and (2) can apply to the information` TRUE
#ASSERT `section 101(1) and (2) can apply to the information` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 102(1) to (4) can apply to the information` TRUE
#ASSERT `section 102(1) to (4) can apply to the information` FALSE

§ `126D -- disobeying a direction`

#ASSERT `the employer has committed the section 126D(2) offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the employer has committed the section 126D(2) offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the maximum fine for disobeying a section 126D direction` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment in months for disobeying a section 126D direction` EQUALS 6

§ `126C(6) -- stay of enforcement`

#ASSERT `enforcement of the administrative penalty is stayed` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `enforcement of the administrative penalty is stayed` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `enforcement of the administrative penalty is stayed` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `enforcement of the administrative penalty is stayed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `2(1) -- whose retrenchment counts`

#ASSERT `is an employee for the purposes of the Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is an employee for the purposes of the Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is an employee for the purposes of the Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is an employee for the purposes of the Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
